From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:34:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Give each VM one compute pool and
 descriptor by default

Make mode 2 of g16_compute_shared_pool the default: one 32 MiB UMA
pool, one allocator descriptor, one submitted counter and UMA index 1
per VM, shared by all its compute units, as macOS has.

Mode 1, the default from 1.1009 to 1.1051, shared one pool under 16
per-unit descriptors whose saved ring cursors disagreed. The concurrent
render and compute stress test (cr.concurrent) failed on every seed on
those kernels from 1.1014 on; 1.985 and 1.1007 pass it, and it passes 3
of 3 with one pool per unit (mode 0, the 1.1052 default). Mode 0 costs
memory: MemAvailable falls by 547 MiB while one compute client runs on
1.1052, against about 38 MiB for one shared pool (measured on 1.1006).
Mode 2 keeps one pool per VM with a single descriptor.

In mode 2 a compute command goes behind running flights only when all
of them belong to its VM. Revert with g16_compute_shared_pool=0 (one
pool per unit) or 1 (the old shared pool).

Measured on an experimental kernel with g16_compute_shared_pool=2 set at
boot: the concurrent render and compute stress test and the deep-queue
stress test (queue.depth) both pass on 3 of 3 seeds, with 57,560 to
58,232 and 71,940 to 72,198 checked results and no GPU fault. The
deep-queue test fails on 3 of 3 seeds in modes 0 and 1. MemAvailable
falls by 72 MiB while one compute client runs, against 547 MiB in mode
0. Light compute takes 35.5 us per job against 37.7 us in mode 0; light
drawing reads 87.2 us against 86.2 us, heavy compute 558.0 us against
557.4 us and heavy drawing 249.7 us against 250.1 us.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index aa4d9f80a0..b6c9dfa39d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -854,8 +854,8 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_units() -> usize {
     "G16: compute units per VM, one compute command in flight each (default 16; 2..16; 12 = k948; 8 = before; 4 = k908; 9..16 = deeper compute queue, ~33 MiB per unit, 13..16 for g16_horizon up to 15; latched at the engine start, set it as a module option)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_shared_pool` (0644, default 0; latched at its first read).
-static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_shared_pool` (0644, default 2; latched at its first read).
+static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(2);
 /// 0 until latched, then 1 (mode 0), 2 (mode 1) or 3 (mode 2).
 static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL_LATCH: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
 
@@ -903,7 +903,7 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_shared_pool_state() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL_PARM,
     COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL,
     "g16_compute_shared_pool",
-    "G16: 0 (default) = one 32 MiB UMA pool per compute unit; 1 = all compute units of a VM allocate from unit 0's pool, each keeping its own allocator descriptor and UMA index; 2 = one pool AND one allocator descriptor, counter and UMA index per VM, shared by all its compute units, as macOS has; latched at the engine start, set it as a module option"
+    "G16: 0 = one 32 MiB UMA pool per compute unit; 1 = all compute units of a VM allocate from unit 0's pool, each keeping its own allocator descriptor and UMA index; 2 (default) = one pool AND one allocator descriptor, counter and UMA index per VM, shared by all its compute units, as macOS has; latched at the engine start, set it as a module option"
 );
 
 live_u32_param!(
